WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.550
From above, the edge of the
Amazon is a ragged line,

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.110
where forest meets cleared land.

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.030
It's the largest tropical
rainforest on Earth,

4
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.390
with about 16,000 tree species.

5
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:17.650
Most of it is in Brazil, but it reaches
into eight other countries and territories.

6
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.850
Clearing in Brazil's Amazon
has been recorded since 1988.

7
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.370
So who is clearing it?

8
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.190
And why should anyone beyond Brazil care?

9
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.110
In this mission, you'll read the
record of clearing year by year,

10
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.970
and calculate how fast it has changed.

11
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.510
Then you'll trace what
replaces the forest,

12
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.410
and weigh up the impacts.

13
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.590
Your mission: find out who
is clearing the Amazon,

14
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.080
and why it matters far beyond Brazil.
